A comment whose `;` lands mid-sentence; the next line begins with two
adjacent bare identifiers, which no SSL statement can start with. The
stranded text does not parse, so comment_text_after_terminator reports one
error at the comment's `;` and the parse-level rules defer (issues #25,
#343).
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE MergeAddresses;
	:PARAMETERS oAddress;
	/* Treat the address as one composite value;
	   if any component changes the whole record is resent;
	:RETURN oAddress;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE MergeAddresses;
	:PARAMETERS oAddress;

	/* Treat the address as one composite value;
	if any component changes the whole record is resent;

	:RETURN oAddress;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
3:45-3:46 error comment_text_after_terminator: The comment ends at this ';', and the text after it is not SSL. The first ';' ends a comment, so the rest is parsed as code; remove the ';' from the comment text
